{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine the maximum area of the rectangular playground that Richard can build with 200 feet of fencing, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Define the variables:**\n   Let \\( L \\) be the length of the rectangle and \\( W \\) be the width of the rectangle.\n\n2. **Set up the perimeter equation:**\n   The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n   \\[\n   P = 2L + 2W\n   \\]\n   Since Richard has 200 feet of fencing, we have:\n   \\[\n   2L + 2W = 200\n   \\]\n   Simplify this equation by dividing everything by 2:\n   \\[\n   L + W = 100\n   \\]\n\n3. **Express one variable in terms of the other:**\n   Solve for \\( W \\) in terms of \\( L \\):\n   \\[\n   W = 100 - L\n   \\]\n\n4. **Write the area equation:**\n   The area \\( A \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n   \\[\n   A = L \\times W\n   \\]\n   Substitute \\( W \\) from the previous step:\n   \\[\n   A = L \\times (100 - L)\n   \\]\n   Simplify the expression:\n   \\[\n   A = 100L - L^2\n   \\]\n\n","prefix_end":915,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,279,7192,3082,315,279,51424,41615,429,11867,646,1936,448,220,17,15,15,7541,315,67427,11,582,1184,311,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,35338,279,7332,25,1019,256,6771,17767,444,1124,8,387,279,3084,315,279,22756,323,17767,467,1124,8,387,279,2374,315,279,22756,382,17,13,3070,1649,705,279,46342,23606,25,1019,256,576,46342,17767,393,1124,8,315,264,22756,374,2661,553,510,256,1124,9640,256,393,284,220,17,43,488,220,17,54,198,256,1124,921,256,8704,11867,702,220,17,15,15,7541,315,67427,11,582,614,510,256,1124,9640,256,220,17,43,488,220,17,54,284,220,17,15,15,198,256,1124,921,256,61242,1437,419,23606,553,49702,4297,553,220,17,510,256,1124,9640,256,444,488,467,284,220,16,15,15,198,256,1124,2533,18,13,3070,8504,825,3890,304,3793,315,279,1008,25,1019,256,63284,369,17767,467,1124,8,304,3793,315,17767